[Music]  danny vilnav's dune was definitely one  of the hits of this movie year still the  blockbuster based on the book series of  the same name by frank herbert in fact  only showed part of what we know from  the original books today we want to talk  about dune part 2 and over a small  preview of the sequel which will be  groundbreaking for the further  development of the dune franchise we'll  cover lots of events from the books from  theatrical film and from david lynch's  old movie so of course there is a  correspondingly high risk of spoilers  in dune we were already introduced to  the gigantic universe during the almost  two and a half hour duration the story  takes place in the year  10191 and deals with the power struggle  for control over the galactic empire of  mankind the focus is on paul atreides a  smart young man who cannot quite grasp  yet what his great destiny will turn out  to be the son of lady jessica and  ukulele to atreyus first is not really  finding his way around his new home  planet of erikas and is soon confronted  with the death of his father and his  escape with his mother from the forces  of the hostile harkonnen family at the  end of the film he meets the girl johnny  whom he had previously only seen in his  dreams and joins the native freeman the  ending of part one is not as a prop as  it might seem at first glance given a  large scale story the first movie  covered roughly half of herbert's book  dune and concludes when halsey trades  his moral as non-existent and looks like  an outnumbered battle a ritual by which  paul and his mother gain the respect of  the freeman has already been depicted in  the film paul fights james in a knife  fight to the death as the laws of the  freeman demand the second ritual on the  other hand did not occur which is why we  assume that we will see it at the  beginning of dune 2. this time is the  turn of paul's mother jessica as she has  to drink from the water of life however  contrary to its euphoria's name the  water of life is not a tasty magic  potion but the poisonous excretion of a  young said warm ground in water the  procedure has to do with the beliefs of  the fremen because worms play a major  role there they're characterized by  great duality since the warm can  represent both god and satan by drinking  the water she becomes the reverent  mother of the fremen a kind of spiritual  leader as reverend mother she must then  transform the water of life into a  harmless drug that the fremen enjoy to  consume at their gatherings but how does  the story go on in dune 2. those who  know the books will know that after  jessica's ritual there is a big time  jump here director of olaf should be  particularly careful not to rush the  story  after all that was one of the major  flaws of the first movie adaption from  1984 so it may well be that they will  take their time to depict the arrival  and further life of paul and jessica  with the fremen in particular we have in  mind the birth of paul's sister alia who  has already gained consciousness in her  mother's womb through the water ritual  and possesses special powers she is also  the girl with the blue eyes of whom paul  has some visions because of his  successful fight against james paul is  called usual by tripolita stilgar it is  translated as the strength of the base  of the pillar stillger will later become  a loyal companion and important advisor  to the main character the final  acceptance by the fremen is then also  expressed in a completely new name for  paul and that is  in contrast to usual this is his common  name with which everyone addresses him  from now on actually in arabic a similar  word means teacher a second story aspect  that unfortunately comes up far too  short in the book is the initial love  affair between paul and shani which also  took its course during the great time  jump one could certainly fill hours with  the unfolding of the relationship  between paul and shauni up until the  birth of their first child however the  challenge will be to find the balance  between a debunked love story and  interesting story details either way the  book picks up quite late after the time  jump in addition to his personal family  happiness paul grows more and more into  a leader position among the fremen and  his initially not yet developed strength  also becomes increasingly powerful he is  seen by the feminist the great savior  that has been repeatedly prophesied to  them and many of the visions that have  long haunted paul will also eventually  coalesce particularly with all the spies  the freeman consumed paul's powers  continue to increase as a result paul  becomes sort of overpowering and is  capable of looking into the past and the  future as well as seeing all the events  of the universe at the same time it will  be a special treat to see paul riding  the true fan favorites later in the film  namely the sand worms when he then also  drinks the water of life which can  actually only be survived by women his  powers will complete and he will be  ready to finally face baron harkenen  interesting is the future of the  character gurney helg embodied by thanos  actor josh brolin the duke's umura is  also paul's trainer and has trained him  for the adverse conditions of the desert  planet similar to the mantid thuberhavat  it is unclear whether and how they  survived the harkonnen's insidious  attack in the book the method is later  forced into service by baron harkin as  his own mounted peter debris was in fact  killed by duke later due to a mix-up a  different fate happens to gurney as he  surprisingly survives the big battle and  devotes himself to alive as a spy  smuggler in the course of the story he  also meets paul and jessica again who  let's say he's not too fond of  particularly with the letter he finds  himself at odds there are of course more  presumed dead characters with  questionable destinies on the one hand  there is planetary ecologist lead kinds  who appears for the first time as a  woman in vilnav's film adaption unlike  in the book and in the 1984 film  according to the book she is indeed dead  but then again the question can be  raised whether will enough perhaps  recast her for the reason of having her  appear in the second part as well in any  case the director can be credited with  that much artistic freedom in a movie  adaption that is otherwise very close to  the book even more likely is a  reappearance of duncan idaho who was  possibly merely wounded but not killed  in the attack on ericus the likable  character who is also played by the  popular jason mamoa at least appears to  have a future in the world imagined by  frank herbert he no longer appears on  the old dune film but he does celebrate  his return as gola in the second book  strictly speaking however duncan is no  longer alive because agola is an  artificially created human being who  preserves the memories of an individual  and thus lets him live on in a certain  way someone who was missing from the  book as shadow iv the emperor of the  entire universe and undoubtedly one of  the most powerful figures perhaps vilna  deliberately withholds him from us in  order to then abruptly seek him on paul  and his companions as a new villain the  comparison to david lynch's movie is  interesting here because there the  emperor has a normal appearance anyhow  quite a few casting possibilities are  circulating on the net from michael  fassbender and jared harris to match  mikkelsen or ralph vines this slim  elegant man with a cold eyes described  in the book would be perfectly suited  for many actors but there is no reliable  information about casting yet all things  considered it can be said that dune part  1 takes place in a relatively short  period of time compared to the possible  plot of part 2. the difficulty with the  sequel is making a meaningful connection  between the end of the first movie and  the beginning of the second between paul  and jessica's joining the freman and the  big attack on the parent or even the  emperor later on a fair amount of time  passes in between will never has to  accommodate a giant plethora of events  or at least cut them down enough in  order to do justice to the scope of the  book and an adequate big screen  adventure at the same time jessica has  to face the ritual paul becomes muad  deep and learns to ride sandworms and  then simultaneously they have to prepare  for the grand finale of the second part  and include many of the aforementioned  characters anyway we are very excited  about tuned part 2 and look forward to  the planned release in almost 2 years  time on october 20th 2023  this was our latest original on dune  part 2. what do you expect from the  sequel do you agree with our analysis  and most importantly who would you like  to see in the role of the mighty emperor  feel free to let us know in the comment  section see you next time  [Music]  [Music]

